Zeus provides standard control flow constructs for conditional execution and iteration.

## If Statements

### Basic If

Execute code conditionally:

```zeus
function main(): i32 {
  let age: i32 = 20;

  if (age >= 18) {
    return 1;  // Adult
  }

  return 0;  // Minor
}
```

### If-Else

Handle both branches:

```zeus
function main(): i32 {
  let score: i32 = 75;

  if (score >= 60) {
    return 1;  // Pass
  } else {
    return 0;  // Fail
  }
}
```

### Nested If-Else

Chain multiple conditions:

```zeus
function getGrade(score: i32): i32 {
  if (score >= 90) {
    return 4;  // A
  } else {
    if (score >= 80) {
      return 3;  // B
    } else {
      if (score >= 70) {
        return 2;  // C
      } else {
        if (score >= 60) {
          return 1;  // D
        } else {
          return 0;  // F
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

function main(): i32 {
  return getGrade(85);  // Returns 3 (B)
}
```

## Conditions

Conditions must evaluate to `boolean`:

```zeus
let x: i32 = 10;
let y: i32 = 20;

// Comparison operators
if (x == y) { }   // Equal
if (x != y) { }   // Not equal
if (x < y) { }    // Less than
if (x <= y) { }   // Less than or equal
if (x > y) { }    // Greater than
if (x >= y) { }   // Greater than or equal

// Boolean values
let flag: boolean = true;
if (flag) { }

// Negation
if (!flag) { }
```

## While Loops

Repeat while a condition is true:

```zeus
function main(): i32 {
  let i: i32 = 0;
  let sum: i32 = 0;

  while (i < 10) {
    sum = sum + i;
    i = i + 1;
  }

  return sum;  // Returns 45 (0+1+2+...+9)
}
```

### Counting Loop

```zeus
function factorial(n: i32): i32 {
  let result: i32 = 1;
  let i: i32 = 1;

  while (i <= n) {
    result = result * i;
    i = i + 1;
  }

  return result;
}

function main(): i32 {
  return factorial(5);  // Returns 120
}
```

### Conditional Loop

```zeus
function findFirstPositive(arr: i32[], size: i32): i32 {
  let i: i32 = 0;

  while (i < size) {
    if (arr.get(i) > 0) {
      return arr.get(i);
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }

  return 0;  // Not found
}
```

## Control Flow Patterns

### Early Return

Exit a function early when a condition is met:

```zeus
function isEven(n: i32): boolean {
  if (n == 0) {
    return true;
  }

  // More complex check could go here
  let remainder: i32 = n - (n / 2) * 2;
  return remainder == 0;
}
```

### Accumulator Pattern

Build up a result through iteration:

```zeus
function sumArray(arr: i32[], length: i32): i32 {
  let sum: i32 = 0;
  let i: i32 = 0;

  while (i < length) {
    sum = sum + arr.get(i);
    i = i + 1;
  }

  return sum;
}
```

### Search Pattern

Find an element in a collection:

```zeus
function contains(arr: i32[], length: i32, target: i32): boolean {
  let i: i32 = 0;

  while (i < length) {
    if (arr.get(i) == target) {
      return true;
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }

  return false;
}
```

### Counter Pattern

Count occurrences:

```zeus
function countPositive(arr: i32[], length: i32): i32 {
  let count: i32 = 0;
  let i: i32 = 0;

  while (i < length) {
    if (arr.get(i) > 0) {
      count = count + 1;
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }

  return count;
}
```

## Nested Loops

Loops can be nested for multi-dimensional iteration:

```zeus
function multiplicationTable(): i32 {
  let sum: i32 = 0;
  let i: i32 = 1;

  while (i <= 5) {
    let j: i32 = 1;

    while (j <= 5) {
      sum = sum + (i * j);
      j = j + 1;
    }

    i = i + 1;
  }

  return sum;
}
```

## Practical Examples

### Fibonacci

```zeus
function fibonacci(n: i32): i32 {
  if (n <= 1) {
    return n;
  }

  let prev: i32 = 0;
  let curr: i32 = 1;
  let i: i32 = 2;

  while (i <= n) {
    let next: i32 = prev + curr;
    prev = curr;
    curr = next;
    i = i + 1;
  }

  return curr;
}

function main(): i32 {
  return fibonacci(10);  // Returns 55
}
```

### Maximum Value

```zeus
function findMax(arr: i32[], length: i32): i32 {
  if (length == 0) {
    return 0;
  }

  let max: i32 = arr.get(0);
  let i: i32 = 1;

  while (i < length) {
    if (arr.get(i) > max) {
      max = arr.get(i);
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }

  return max;
}
```

<Aside type="note">
  Zeus currently supports `while` loops. `for` loops and other iteration constructs are planned for future releases.
</Aside>

